.Dd May 18, 2026
.Dt GROUPS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm groups
.Nd print group memberships for a user
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar user ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
With no operand,
.Nm
prints the group memberships of the calling process \(em the primary
group (the
.Vt egid )
followed by every supplementary group from
.Xr getgroups 2 ,
each resolved to a name via
.Xr getgrgid 3
where possible.
.Pp
With one or more
.Ar user
operands,
.Nm
walks
.Pa /etc/group
and prints, for each user, the primary group named in
.Pa /etc/passwd
followed by every group that lists the user in its supplementary-member
roll.
.Pp
When more than one
.Ar user
is given, each line is prefixed with
.Dq Ar user No \&: .
.Sh OUTPUT
A single line per user, space-separated group names.  GIDs that have
no corresponding name in
.Pa /etc/group
are printed as the bare integer.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
At least one named user did not exist, or
.Xr getgroups 2
failed.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Pa /etc/passwd
.It Pa /etc/passwd
Primary-group lookup.
.It Pa /etc/group
Supplementary-group iteration.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr id 1 ,
.Xr getgroups 2 ,
.Xr getgrent 3 ,
.Xr getpwnam 3 ,
.Xr group 5 ,
.Xr passwd 5
.Sh AUTHORS
The
.Nm
utility was written for substrate.
